{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' openspec/changes/case-insensitive-template-autoescape/proposal.md\nsed -n '1,260p' openspec/changes/case-insensitive-template-autoescape/specs/template-autoescape/spec.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Proposal\n\n## Why\n\nFlask's default Jinja autoescape selector only recognizes lowercase template\nsuffixes, so templates such as `invoice.HTML` and `diagram.SvG` render without\nthe protection provided to their lowercase equivalents. Template filenames are\ncommonly case-insensitive at the extension level, and this discrepancy is\nsurprising and unsafe.\n\n## What Changes\n\n- Make Flask's default Jinja autoescape selection recognize its supported\n  template extensions regardless of filename case.\n- Preserve existing behavior for unsupported extensions and unnamed templates.\n- Add regression coverage for uppercase and mixed-case supported extensions.\n\n## Capabilities\n\n### New Capabilities\n- `template-autoescape`: Default autoescaping decisions for Flask template\n  filenames.\n\n### Modified Capabilities\n\nNone.\n\n## Impact\n\nThis affects `Flask.select_jinja_autoescape` in `src/flask/sansio/app.py` and\nthe templating tests. No public API signatures or dependencies change.\n# Spec Delta\n\n## Purpose\n\nDefines predictable default autoescaping for supported Flask template filenames.\n\n## ADDED Requirements\n\n### Requirement: Case-insensitive supported template extensions\nThe default template autoescaping policy SHALL enable autoescaping for a\ntemplate filename whose extension is HTML, HTM, XML, XHTML, or SVG regardless\nof the letter case used in that extension.\n\n#### Scenario: Uppercase supported extension\n- **WHEN** a template is named `invoice.HTML`\n- **THEN** the default autoescaping policy enables autoescaping\n\n#### Scenario: Mixed-case supported extension\n- **WHEN** a template is named `diagram.SvG`\n- **THEN** the default autoescaping policy enables autoescaping\n\n### Requirement: Existing non-supported and unnamed behavior\nThe default template autoescaping policy SHALL continue to disable autoescaping\nfor filenames without a supported extension and enable it when no filename is\nprovided.\n\n#### Scenario: Unsupported extension\n- **WHEN** a template is named `report.txt`\n- **THEN** the default autoescaping policy disables autoescaping\n\n#### Scenario: Unnamed template\n- **WHEN** no template filename is provided\n- **THEN** the default autoescaping policy enables autoescaping\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
